$DATUM A. General Procedure. To a round bottom flask was added α-aryl-γ-lactam
6i (1 equiv) and triphenylphosphine (1.5 equiv). To this mixture was
added toluene. The reaction mixture was heated to 80 °C. After 2h, the
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, and the volatiles were
removed in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate and poured
into water. The resulting mixture was extracted by 2 × 5 mL of ethyl
acetate. The combined organic phases were washed with brine. The
resulting organic phase was dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and the filtrate
was concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue by MPLC afforded
3H-pyrroloindoline 7. 3H-Indole 7i. The general procedure was followed by
using 0.124 g of α-aryl-γ-lactam 6i (0.332 mmol), 0.130 g of
triphenylphosphine (0.496 mmol) and 3 mL toluene. Purification by MPLC
(0:100 - 30:70 EtOAc: hexanes). The product as a white solid (0.100 g,
92%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.32 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (t, J =
7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.19 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.07 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (q,
J = 7.0, 2H), 4.06 - 3.97 (m, 2H), 2.58 - 2.52 (m, 1H), 2.37 - 2.31 (m,
1H), 1.54 (s, 9H), 1.40 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
177.5 (C), 169.1 (C), 153.8 (C), 150.2 (C), 136.6 (C), 129.4 (CH), 124.1
(CH), 121.6 (CH), 118.8 (CH), 83.7 (C), 66.2 (CH2), 62.4 (C), 44.1 (CH2),
28.0 (CH3), 27.2 (CH2), 14.3 (CH3); ATR-FTIR (thin film): 3247, 2980,
1702, 1579, 1457, 1321, 1274, 1169, 1018, 758, 668 cm-1. HRMS (EI) m/z
calcd for C18H23N2O4 [M+H]+: 331.1658, found 331.1656.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
