$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-2-(3,4-methylenedioxyphenyl)-4-(4
chlorobenzyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e]-[1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide 6q,
(191 mg, 91%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 169-170 °C; 1H NMR
(400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.92 (dd, J = 1.2 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.63-7.58
(m, 1H, HAr), 7.50-7.37 (m, 2H, HAr), 7.27-7.03 (m, 6H, HAr), 6.69 (dd, J
= 1.2 Hz, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, HAr), 5.99 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.98 (d, J =
1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H), 5.06 (s, 1H), 4.95 (d, J = 14.4
Hz, 1H), 4.65 (d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 3.24-3.17 (m, 1H), 1.41-0.81 (m, 8H),
0.58-0.45 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.4 (Cq), 164.2 (Cq),
163.3 (Cq), 150.4 (Cq), 148.2 (Cq), 146.0 (Cq), 134.8 (Cq), 134.1 (Cq),
132.8 (Cq), 132.0 (CHAr), 131.9 (CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 130.3 (CHAr), 129.0
(CHAr), 128.5 (CHAr), 127.0 (CHAr), 126.1 (CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 122.6
(CHAr), 107.8 (CHAr), 107.6 (CHAr), 101.8 (CH2), 59.2 (CH), 52.1 (CH2),
48.1 (CH), 32.2 (CH2), 32.1 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2);
IR(KBr) ν̃ 3330 (NH), 3063 (CHAr), 2932, 2839, 1690 (C=O), 1614 (C=N),
1505; EIMS m/z 529 (M+, 25), 406 (35), 405 (32), 404 (100), 279 (80), 253
(24), 252 (21), 125 (57); HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H28N3O4Cl: 529.1768;
found 529.1768; Anal. Calcd for C30H28N3O4Cl: C, 67.98; H, 5.33; N, 7.93.
Found: C, 68.11; H, 5.42; N, 8.06.
