$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-methoxybenzyl)-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6k, (187 mg, 91%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 170-171 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.91 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.65 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
2H, HAr), 7.43-7.39 (m, 1H, HAr), 7.28-7.16 (m, 4H, HAr), 6.82 (d, J =
8.8 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.69 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.18 (s, 1H), 5.03-4.99
(m, 2H), 4.46 (d, J = 14.1 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.67 (s, 3H), 3.17-3.10
(m, 1H), 1.37-0.87 (m, 8H), 0.53-0.37 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ
167.4 (Cq), 164.6 (Cq), 163.7 (Cq), 162.0 (Cq), 159.6 (Cq), 146.3 (Cq),
132.0 (CHAr), 130.6 (CHAr), 130.3 (CHAr), 129.4 (CHAr), 128.4 (CHAr),
127.0 (CHAr), 125.9 (CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 114.5 (CHAr), 114.0 (CHAr), 58.5
(CH), 55.4 (CH3), 55.2 (CH3), 52.0 (CH2), 47.9 (CH), 32.2 (CH2), 32.1
(CH2), 25.2 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3326 (NH), 3058
(CHAr), 2929, 2852, 1674 (C=O), 1621 (C=N), 1593, 1514; EIMS m/z 511 (M+,
20), 386 (28), 265 (58), 209 (20), 121 (100); HRMS (EI) calcd for
C31H33N3O4: 511.2471; found 511.2473; Anal. Calcd for C31H33N3O4: C,
72.78; H, 6.50; N, 8.21. Found: C, 72.84; H, 6.42; N, 8.15.
