$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Staudinger Ligation of substrates 9a-9i. To a
solution of diphenylphosphine proline phenyl ester 3b in 3:1
DMF-phosphate buffer (pH 7.4) was added 1.1 equiv. of the corresponding
azido amino acid or peptide in the same solvent system at room
temperature. The final concentration of 3b was 0.1~ 0.08 M. The reaction
was completed usually within 30 min at room temperature. Work-up
procedure was the same as mentioned before. Purification by flash column
chromatography with 3~ 10 % MeOH in DCM gave the desired products.
Compound 9z, white solid, yield 91%. mp 53-57 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 8.38 (t, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 7.99 (s, 1H), 7.64 (m, 2H), 7.52 (m, 2H),
7.47 - 7.32 (m, 5H), 7.32 - 7.07 (m, 12H), 6.93 - 6.76 (m, 2H), 4.89 (dt,
J = 9.7, 6.2 Hz, 1H), 4.58 - 4.32 (m, 2H), 3.97 (td, J = 6.7, 4.3 Hz,
1H), 3.44 - 3.23 (m, 1H), 3.17 - 3.02 (m, 2H), 2.94 (m, 1H), 2.16 - 2.00
(m, 2H), 1.83 - 1.64 (m, 1H), 1.52 (m, 1H); 31P NMR (122 MHz, CDCl3) δ
30.15; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.68, 171.24, 138.77, 136.81, 132.87,
132.83, 132.71, 132.68, 132.35, 132.23, 131.91, 131.77, 129.70, 129.67,
129.14, 128.83, 128.53, 128.34, 127.17, 127.14, 119.88, 115.74, 62.00,
61.96, 53.57, 49.93, 43.74, 43.71, 38.20, 32.14, 32.06,
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phosphate buffered solution used, Staudinger ligation
