$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Staudinger Ligation of
substrates 9a-9i. To a solution of diphenylphosphine proline phenyl ester
3b in 3:1 DMF-phosphate buffer (pH 7.4) was added 1.1 equiv. of the
corresponding azido amino acid or peptide in the same solvent system at
room temperature. The final concentration of 3b was 0.1~ 0.08 M. The
reaction was completed usually within 30 min at room temperature. Work-up
procedure was the same as mentioned before. Purification by flash column
chromatography with 3~ 10 % MeOH in DCM gave the desired products.
Compound 9c, colorless oil, yield 91%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.00 (t,
J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 7.89 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 7.70 (m, 4H), 7.59 - 7.12 (m,
16H), 5.23 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H), 5.03 (s, 2H), 4.47 (m, 3H, CH2Ph
overlapped with Lys(Hα )), 4.04 (ddd, J = 8.3, 5.6, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 3.19 -
3.10 (m, 4H, Pro(Hδ ) overlapped with Lys(Hε )), 2.27 (m, 1H), 2.16 -
1.69 (m, 5H), 1.52 (m, 2H), 1.38 (m, 2H); 31P NMR (122 MHz, CDCl3) δ
29.34; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.04, 171.71, 156.74, 138.85, 136.91,
132.75, 132.71, 132.34, 132.21, 132.13, 131.99, 129.32, 129.16, 129.03,
128.99, 128.70, 128.67, 128.26, 128.20, 128.06, 127.33, 66.66, 62.40,
62.36, 53.67, 49.17, 43.59, 40.71, 32.19, 31.70, 29.34, 25.49, 25.40,
22.83; IR (thin film) 3293.1, 3060.2, 2941.7, 2864.0, 1699.4, 1651.4,
1523.7, 1437.9, 1249.3, 735.1, 694.2 cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C38H44N4O5P [M+H]+ 667.3, found 667.2 .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phosphate buffered solution used, Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A proline-based phosphine template for Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Park, Chung-Min; Niu, Wei; Liu, Chunrong; Biggs, Tyler D.; Guo, Jiantao;
Xian, Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(17), 4694-4697

