$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A. General Procedure. To a round bottom flask
was added α-aryl-γ-lactam 6i (1 equiv) and triphenylphosphine (1.5
equiv). To this mixture was added toluene. The reaction mixture was
heated to 80 °C. After 2h, the reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, and the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in ethyl acetate and poured into water. The resulting mixture
was extracted by 2 × 5 mL of ethyl acetate. The combined organic phases
were washed with brine. The resulting organic phase was dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and the filtrate was concentrated in vacuo.
Purification of the residue by MPLC afforded 3H-pyrroloindoline 7.
3H-Indole 7i. The general procedure was followed by using 0.124 g of
α-aryl-γ-lactam 6i (0.332 mmol), 0.130 g of triphenylphosphine (0.496
mmol) and 3 mL toluene. Purification by MPLC (0:100 - 30:70 EtOAc:
hexanes). 3H-Indole 7g. The general procedure was followed by using 0.024
g of β-ketoester 6g (0.086 mmol), 0.034 g of triphenylphosphine (0.258
mmol) and 2 mL toluene. Purification by MPLC (0:100 - 30:70 EtOAc:
hexanes). The product as a yellow solid (0.018 g, 90%). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.39 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.20 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (t, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.36
(d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.24 - 4.21 (m, 1H), 4.01 (td, J = 11.0, 1.0 Hz,
1H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 2.94 - 2.87 (m, 1H), 2.65 (td, J = 15.0, 3.0 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 200.3 (C), 169.8 (C), 138.2 (C), 129.6 (CH),
129.3 (CH), 126.2 (C), 125.2 (CH), 119.4 (CH), 73.5 (CH2), 67.9 (CH2),
67.2 (C), 53.3 (CH3), 40.9 (CH2); ATR-FTIR (thin film): 2956, 2854, 1732,
1585, 1454, 1246, 1212, 1166, 1078, 1045, 947, 835, 772, 735 cm-1. HRMS
(EI) m/z calcd for C13H14NO3 [M+H]+: 232.0974, found 232.0972.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Synthesis of 3H-Indoles Enabled by the Lead-Mediated
α-Arylation of β-Ketoesters or γ-Lactams Using Aryl Azides
