$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N,N'-Phenylenebistri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine imide,
N,N'-Phenylene-Bis-tri(p- Methoxyphenyl)Phosphine Imide, 1b: Following
air free techniques, to 500 mg (3.13 mmol) of 1,4-diazidobenzene
dissolved in 25 mL of dry benzene was added via canula 2.32 g (6.25 mmol)
of tri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine dissolved in 20 mL of benzene. The
reaction mixture was stirred under nitrogen for four hours. N2 was
evolved and a yellow solid precipitated from solution during the reaction
period. To enhance the precipitation of this solid, the benzene solution
was added dropwise via canula to 20 mL of dry ether. The solid was
filtered and dried under vacuum to give
N,N'-Phenylenebistri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine imide,
N,N'-Phenylene-Bis-tri(p- Methoxyphenyl)Phosphine Imide, yield 2.28 g ,
2.81 mmol, 90 % . (mp: 219-220 °C).1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.81 (s,
18H, CH3), 6.85 (d, 12H, J = 7.8), 7.34 (s, 4H), 7.57 (dd, 12H, J = 11.9,
J = 7.8). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 55.4, 114.0 (d,JC-P = 12.6), 134.6
(d, JC-P = 10.1), 128.4, 161.9. 31P NMR (162 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.0. FTIR
(Reflectance, cm-1): 3022, 3004, 2965, 2930, 2836, 1593, 1495, 1286,
1251, 1174, 1101, 1042, 825, 799.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
