$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of Azide derivatives with TPPc in
Table 2 Azide derivatives 9a-9g (1 equiv) and 2 (1.1 equiv) were
dissolved in THF-H2O (5 mL, 9:1, v/v). A mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 2 h and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel to give primary amino derivatives
10a-10g. 0.1M concentration of azide derivatives in the reaction solvent
was used in this study. 9a, 10a, 10b: Commercially available
3-aminophenol 10b 1H-NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 8.79 (1H, s), 6.76 (1H, t, J =
8.24), 5.98-5.96 (2H, m), 5.91 (1H, m), 4.86 (2H, s)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
