$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-2-(3,4-methylenedioxyphenyl)-4-(4
methylbenzyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e]-[1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide 6g,
(182 mg, 90%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 193-194 °C; 1H NMR
(400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.96 (dd, J = 1.4 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.49-7.17
(m, 7H, HAr), 7.08 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.78 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H,
HAr), 6.02 (s, 2H), 5.18 (s, 1H), 5.16 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (d, J =
8.2 Hz, 1H), 4.46 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.17-3.12 (m, 1H), 2.29 (s, 3H),
1.41-0.93 (m, 8H), 0.53-0.40 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.3
(Cq), 164.5 (Cq), 163.4 (Cq), 150.3 (Cq), 148.3 (Cq), 146.2 (Cq), 138.4
(Cq), 133.4 (CHAr), 132.4 (Cq), 132.0 (CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 129.9 (CHAr),
129.0 (CHAr), 127.0 (CHAr), 125.9 (CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 122.7 (CHAr), 107.8
(CHAr), 107.8 (CHAr), 101.7 (CH2), 58.8 (CH), 52.3 (CH2), 47.9 (CH), 32.2
(CH2), 32.0 (CH2), 25.2 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.3 (CH2), 21.0 (CH3); IR
(KBr) ν̃ 3324 (NH), 3003 (CHAr), 2927, 2861, 1674 (C=O), 1619 (C=N),
1511, 1451, 1249; EIMS m/z 509 (M+, 34), 385 (27), 384 (100), 383 (24),
279 (23); HRMS (EI) calcd for C31H31N3O4: 509.2315; found 509.2324; Anal.
Calcd for C31H31N3O4: C, 73.06; H, 6.13; N, 8.25. Found: C, 73.12; H,
6.02; N, 8.29.
