$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 40 (25.7 mg, 0.058 mmol, 1.0
equiv) in tetrahydrofuran (3.0 mL) at 23 °C was added triphenylphosphine
( 16.8 m g, 0.0 64 mmol, 1.1 equiv). The solution was stirred at 23 °C
for 10 min and then concentrated. The residue was agitated and washed
with ether to afford the corresponding triphenylphosphine imide as a
white powder ( 39.7 mg ). To a solution of the triphenylphosphine imide
(39.7 mg, 0.059 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in tetrahydrofurn (8.0 mL) at 0 °C was
added m-chloroperbenzoic acid (15.2 mg, 0.088 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in small
portions. The reaction was stirred at 0 °C for 12 h before quenched with
10% sodium thiosulfate/saturated sodium bicarbonate (1:1 v/v, 20 mL). The
solvent was then removed by rotary evaporator. The residue was dissolved
in ethyl acetate (10 mL), washed with saturated sodium bicarbonate,
brine, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated.
The crude product was then washed by ether for three times to afford 41.
White powder, yield (36.0 mg, 90% for two steps). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.83-7.75 (m, 6H), 7.64-7.57 (m, 3H), 7.56-7.45 (m, 6H), 7.24-7.17 (m,
3H), 7.14-7.04 (m, 5H), 7.00 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 5.00 (d, J = 10.8 Hz,
1H),4.85 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 4.45 (dd, J = 9.5, 5.5 Hz, 1H,), 4.10 (d,
J = 9.5 Hz, 1H), 3.91 (dd, J = 12.5, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.89 (d, J = 12.5 Hz,
1H), 3.81 (d, J = 12.5 Hz, 1H), 3.31 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 1.69 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 204.0, 177.0, 173.8, 161.0, 138.0, 134.6,
133.4, 133.3, 132.60, 132.57,128.83, 128.78, 128.7, 128.4, 128.25,
128.17, 127.7, 127.43, 127.37, 86.2, 69.5, 68.6, 57.6, 52.5, 44.1, 19.7;
MS(ES)+ calcd for C42H37N3O5P (M+H)+ 694.2, found 694.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Biomimetic Route for Construction of the [4+2] and [3+2] Core Skeletons
of Dimeric Pyrrole-Imidazole Alkaloids and Asymmetric Synthesis of
Ageliferins
