$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds. N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-fluorobenzyl)-2-(3,4
methylenedioxyphenyl)-5-oxo-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e]-[1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6w, (182 mg, 89%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 89-90 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.91 (dd, J = 1.6 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr),
7.45-7.06 (m, 7H, HAr), 6.85 (t, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.70 (d, J = 8.2
Hz, 1H, HAr), 5.97 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H), 5.96 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 1H), 5.09
(s, 1H), 5.06 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.79 (s, 2H), 3.22-3.10 (m, 1H),
1.76-0.88 (m, 8H), 0.56-0.41 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.5
(Cq), 164.3 (Cq), 163.3 (Cq), 162.6 (d, 1J = 247.7 Hz, Cq), 150.4 (Cq),
148.3 (Cq), 146.0 (Cq), 132.2 (d, 4J = 3.4 Hz, Cq), 132.1 (Cq), 132.0
(CHAr), 130.7 (CHAr), 130.6 (d, 3J = 8.8 Hz, CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 127.1
(CHAr), 126.1 (CHAr), 125.8 (CHAr), 122.6 (CHAr), 115.9 (d, 2J = 21.6 Hz,
CH Ar), 107.9 (CHAr), 107.7 (CHAr), 101.8 (CH2), 59.2 (CH), 52.1 (CH2),
48.1 (CH), 32.3 (CH2), 32.2 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2); IR
(KBr) ν̃ 3308 (NH), 3063 (CHAr), 2921, 2839, 1718 (C=O), 1677 (C=O), 1625
(C=N), 1581, 1505, 1451, 1227; EIMS m/z 513 (M+, 21), 388 (100), 279
(72), 109 (99); HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H28N3O4F: 513.2064; found
513.2061; Anal. Calcd for C30H28N3O4F: C, 70.16; H, 5.50; N, 8.18. Found:
C, 70.08; H, 5.59; N, 8.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
