$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of R3PN3Ad (R = iPr, Cy). A 20 mL
scintillation vial was charged with 0.0516 g (0.184 mmol) PCy3 and 0.0328
g (0.185 mmol) N3Ad. 3.0 mL of toluene were added to the vial. Both
solids dissolved readily. The sample was then evacuated to dryness. The
solid was then recrystallized from a mixture of pentane and toluene to
obtain clear colorless crystals suitable for X-ray analysis. The product
was obtained in 68 % yield. Preparation of Me3PNAd. The preparation of
Me3PNAd is similar to the preparation of R3PN3Ad described above. The
product was obtained as a crystalline powder in 89% yield. 1H NMR (C6Dd)
δ (ppm): 1.00 (d, 9H, CH3), 1.94 (m, 6H, Ad CH2), 1.72 (m, 6H, Ad CH2),
2.13 (m, 3H, Ad CH). 13C NMR (C6D6) δ (ppm): 53.4 (d, 1C, Ad C), 50.8 (d,
3C, Ad CH2), 37.9 (s, 3C, Ad CH), 31.6 (s, 3C, Ad CH2), 21.3 (d, 3C,
CH3). 31P NMR (C6D6) δ (ppm): -61.3. FAB+ MS: 226.
