$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dipeptide Boc-(4R-H2N)Pro-Apa-OMe. Boc-(4R-N3)Pro-Apa-OMe (1.42 g, 3.7
mmol) and triphenylphosphine (1.91 g, 7.3 mmol) were dissolved in THF (30
mL). After the addition of water (0.13 mL, 7.3 mmol) the reaction mixture
was heated to reflux for 4 h. The solvent was evaporated and the residue
subjected to column chromatography by using dichloromethane/methanol,
10:1 (v/v) as eluent. Yield 1.17 g (88 %); MS (MALDI-TOF) m/z (%) 365.1
(50) [M+H]+, 387.1 (100) [M+Na]+, 403.1 (22) [M+K]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Recognition of Sulfate Anions by a Cyclopeptide-Derived
Receptor in Aqueous Phosphate Buffer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schaly, Astrid; Belda, Raquel; Garcia-Espana, Enrique; Kubik, Stefan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(24), 6238-6241

