$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 40 (4.9 mg, 0.011 mmol, 1.0
equiv) in tetrahydrofuran (0.65 mL) was added a solution of lithium
hydroxide (0.34 N in water , 0.16 mL, 5.0 equiv) at 23 °C. The reaction
was stirred at 60 °C for 2 h and concentrated. The residue was then
partitioned between ethyl acetate and brine. The layers were separated
and the organic layer was washed with water, brine, dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The crude decarboxylation
product obtained above was then dissolved in tetrahydrofuran (1.0 mL) and
triphenylphosphine (3.2 mg, 0.012 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added. The
solution was stirred at 23 °C for 10 min . T he solvent was then removed
by rotary evaporator and the crude mixture was purified by preparative
HPLC ( Eclipse XDB - C18, 9.4× 250 mm, 5 μm, eluent A: water with 0.1%
trifluoroacetic acid, eluent B: acetonitrile with 0.1% trifluoroacetic
acid, gradient: T = 0 min: 60% B, T = 20 min: 85% B, 4.8 mL/min ) to
afford 42' and 42. Compound 42, yiled 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
