$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-fluorobenzyl)-5-oxo-2-[4
(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e]-[1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6v, (187 mg, 88%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 132-133 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.89 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.63 (d, J = 8.5 Hz,
2H, HAr), 7.50 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H, HAr), 7.45-7.40 (m, 1H, HAr),
7.26-7.10 (m, 4H, HAr), 6.71 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.17 (d, J = 8.5
Hz, 1H), 5.09 (s, 1H), 4.90 (d, J = 14.3 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d, J = 14.3 Hz,
1H), 3.21-3.13 (m, 1H), 1.43-0.35 (m, 10H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ
164.3 (Cq), 164.0 (Cq), 162.9 (d, 1J = 248.6 z, Cq), 145.9 (Cq), 141.2
(Cq), 132.6 (CHAr), 132.7 (q, 2J = 32.6 Hz, Cq), 130.9 (d, 3J = 8.2 Hz,
CHAr), 130.8 (CHAr), 123.9 (q, 1J = 272.5 Hz, Cq), 128.0 (CHAr), 127.5
(CHAr), 127.1 (CHAr), 125.8 (CHAr), 125.7 (q, 4J = 3.7 Hz, Cq), 116.2 (d,
2J = 21.6 Hz, CHAr), 59.9 (CH), 52.4 (CH2), 48.5 (CH), 32.5 (CH2), 25.3
(CH2), 24.9 (CH2), 24.7 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3579, 3478, 3295 (NH), 3065
(CHAr), 2927, 2858, 1659 (C=O), 1621 (C=O), 1511, 1322, 1123; EIMS m/z
537 (M+, 10), 413 (53), 412 (73), 304 (19), 303 (100), 277 (19), 275
(23), 109 (86); HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H27N3O2F4: 537.2039; found
537.2036; Anal. Calcd for C30H27N3O2F4: C, 67.03; H, 5.06; N, 7.82.
Found: C, 66.92; H, 5.13; N, 7.69.
