$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of azide 49 (61.4 mg, 0.090 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in
tetrahydrofuran (2.0 mL) and water (0.50 mL) at 23 °C was added
triphenylphosphine ( 59.1 mg, 0. 226 mmol, 2.5 equiv). The solution was
stirred at 70 °C overnight and then concentrated. T he residue was
partitioned between ethyl acetate (10 mL) and brine (5 mL). The layers
were separated and the organic layer was dried over anhydrous sodium
sulfate, filtered , concentrated , and purified by preparative HPLC
(Waters Atlantis dC18 OBD, 19× 150 mm, 5 μm, eluent A: water, eluent B:
acetonitrile, gradient: T = 0 min: 55 % B, T = 40 min: 80% B, 5.0 mL/min)
to give the corresponding amine. Oil, yield (70.4 mg, 88 %). Retention
time: 19.2 min. MS(ES)+ calcd for C50H62N6O7P (M+H)+ 889.4, found 889.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Biomimetic Route for Construction of the [4+2] and [3+2] Core Skeletons
of Dimeric Pyrrole-Imidazole Alkaloids and Asymmetric Synthesis of
Ageliferins
