$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure B (release as isothiocyanate): The iminophosphorane-loaded
resin was swollen in 10% CS2 in dry DMF (approximately 8 mL per g resin)
under N2 and heated under &#x3BC;w irradiation at 60 &#x00B0;C (2 x 10
min). Then, the resin was filtered and washed with DMF (6 x 2 min) to
obtain the released isothiocyanate. The combined filtrates were
concentrated and freeze-dried in order to determine reaction yield and
product purity.
6I-isothiocyanato-6-II-VII-hexaazido-6I-VII-heptadeoxy-2I-VII,3I-VII-tetradeca-O-methylcyclomaltoheptaose
(11). Monoisothiocyanate 11 was obtained from 3 (153 mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 eq)
and resin 7 (0.15 g, 0.34 mmol·g-1) using the catch-and-release protocol
as described in procedure B in 86% yield (67 mg). HPLC: tR = 13.7 min; Rf
= 0.55 (4:1 EtOAc-petroleum ether); [&#x3B1;]D = +163.2 (c 0.9, DCM); 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): &#x3B4; 5.11-5.08 (m, 7 H, H-1I-VII), 3.97 (dd, 1
H, J6a,5 = 2.4 Hz, J6a,6b = 14.8 Hz, H-6aI), 3.91 (dd, 1 H, J6a,5 = 5.1
Hz, H-6bI), 3.84-3.65 (m, 7 H, H-5I-VII), 3.84-3.45 (m, 12 H,
H-6a,bII-VI), 3.63 (m, 21 H, OCH3 I-VII) 3.55-3.45 (m, 14 H, H-3I-VII,
H-4I-VII), 3.52 (m, 21 H, OCH3 I-VII), 3.21-3.15 (m, 7 H, H-2I-VII);
1D-TOCSY (500 MHz, CDCl3, H-6aI irradiation): &#x3B4; 5.10 (s, 1 H,
H-1I), 4.04-3.90 (m, 14 H, H-6aI, H-6bI), 3.60-3.40 (m, 2 H, H-3I, H-4I),
3.22 (m, 1 H, H-2I); 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3): &#x3B4; 99.0 (C-1I-VII),
81.9-81.3 (C-2I-VII,C-3I-VII, C-4I-VII), 71.3 (C-5I-VII), 61.9 (OCH3
I-VII), 59.3 (OCH3 I-VII), 52.2 (C-6I-VII); ESI-MS: m/z 1545 [M + Na]+.
Elemental analysis calculated (%) for C57H91N19O28S: C 44.97, H 6.02, N
17.48, S 1.45; found: C 44.71, H 5.90, N 17.31, S 1.86.
