$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N,N'-Phenylenebistri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine
imide, N,N'-Phenylene-Bis-tri(p- Methoxyphenyl)Phosphine Imide, 1b:
Following air free techniques, to 500 mg (3.13 mmol) of
1,4-diazidobenzene dissolved in 25 mL of dry benzene was added via canula
2.32 g (6.25 mmol) of tri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine dissolved in 20 mL of
benzene. The reaction mixture was stirred under nitrogen for four hours.
N2 was evolved and a yellow solid precipitated from solution during the
reaction period. To enhance the precipitation of this solid, the benzene
solution was added dropwise via canula to 20 mL of dry ether. The solid
was filtered and dried under vacuum to give
N,N'-Phenylenebistri(p-methoxyphenyl)phosphine imide,
N,N'-Phenylene-Bis-tri(p- Methoxyphenyl)Phosphine Imide, yield 2.28 g ,
2.81 mmol, 90 % . N,N'-Phenylenebistri(p-methylphenyl)phosphine imide,
1c: yield 85 % . 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.34 (s, 18 H, CH3), 6.48 (s,
4H), 7.15 (dd, 12H,J = 7.14, JH-P = 2.85), 7.56 (t, 12H, JH-P = 11.43, J
= 7.14). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ21.59 (s), 132.78 (d,JC-P = 11.22),
128.3, 129.1 (d,JC-P = 11.6), 125.4, 141.5. 31P-NMR(162 MHz, CDCl3): δ
5.4. FTIR (Reflectance, cm-1): 3020, 3012, 2980, 2920, 2866,1491, 1321,
1277, 1190, 1144, 1103, 1053, 1020, 825 -806, 710, 660, 639, 525 and 451.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bis(phosphine Imide)s: Easily Tunable Organic Electron Donors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
