$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the
Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction: Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was
added under nitrogen to a solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y
(0.4 mmol) in toluene (10 ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at
room temperature. Then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure
and the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
mixtures as eluent). Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from
DEPT, COSY, HMQC and HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c,
both in CDCl3, as model compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-(4-fluorobenzyl)-5-oxo-2-(4-methylphenyl-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6s, (162 mg, 85%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 195-196 °C; 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.95 (dd, J = 1.1 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr), 7.56
(d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H, HAr), 7.48-7.43 (m, 1H, HAr), 7.33-7.22 (m, 4H), 7.13
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H, HAr), 6.82 (t, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H, HAr), 5.20 (s, 1H),
5.14 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.84 (d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 4.77 (d, J = 14.4
Hz, 1H), 3.26-3.17 (m, 1H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 1.48-0.90 (m, 8H), 0.59-0.45
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.6 (Cq), 164.2 (Cq), 164.1 (Cq),
162.4 (d, Cq, 1J = 247.4 Hz, CF), 146.0 (Cq), 141.6 (Cq), 134.6 (Cq),
132.0 (d, 4J= 3.2 Hz, Cq), 131.8 (CHAr), 130.5 (CHAr), 130.4 (CHAr),
129.2 (CHAr), 127.3 (CHAr), 126.9 (CHAr), 126.0 (CHAr), 125.8 (CHAr),
115.6 (d, 2J = 21.6 Hz, CHAr), 59.0 (CH), 51.9 (CH2), 48.0 (CH), 32.1
(CH2), 32.0 (CH2), 24.9 (CH2), 24.4 (CH2), 24.3 (CH2), 21.2 (CH3); IR
(KBr) ν̃ 3298 (NH), 3059 (CHAr), 2920, 2849, 1642 (C=O), 1597, 1539; EIMS
m/z 483 (M+, 7), 358 (46), 278 (47), 277 (100), 249 (24), 201 (22), 109
(37); HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H30N3O2F: 483.2322; found 483.2318; Anal.
Calcd for C30H30N3O2F: C, 74.51; H, 6.25; N, 8.69. Found: C,74.59; H,
6.32; N, 8.59.
