$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
{η5-C5H4-(PPh2dN-2,6-Me2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-PPh2-2-CH(Me)NMe2} (1a). To a
solution of BPPFA (1.00 g, 1.60mmol) in diethyl ether (15 mL) was added
drop wise an equimolar amount of 2,6-dimethylbenzoyl azide (0.24 g,
1.60mmol). Bubbles of N2 gas evolved during the addition. Themixture was
further stirred overnight at ambient temperature, after which time the
solvent was removed. The oily residue dissolved in a minimum amount of
CH2Cl2 was transferred onto a column of silica gel for chromatographic
separation. A single orange band was eluted with a mixture of hexane
andethyl acetate (8:2) to give orange solids after removal of solvents.
Re crystallization from CH2Cl2/hexane yielded 0.49g of 1a in two crops as
yellow solids.
{η5-C5H4-(PPh2=N-2,6-iPr2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-PPh2-2-CH(Me)NMe2} (1b). The
title compound was prepared in the same manner as described above for the
synthesis of 1a, by replacing 2,6-dimethylbenzoyl azide with
2,6-diisopropylbenzoylazide. Yield: 1.08 g (85%). 31P NMR (CDCl3): δ
-23.76 (s, PPh2), -9.11 (s, P=N). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 0.88 (d, J = 6.9, 6H,
CHMe2), 0.96 (d, J = 6.9, 6H, CHMe2), 1.11 (d, J = 6.9, 3H, CHMe),
1.68(s, 6H, NMe2), 3.40 (sept, J = 6.6, 2H, CHMe2), 3.50, 3.63 (br, 4H,
C5H4), 4.02 (qt, J = 4.8, 1H, CHMe), 4.28-4.46 (m, 3H, C5H3), 6.76 (t, J
= 7.5, 1H, p-NC6H3), 6.93 (d, J = 7.5, 2H, M-N-C6H3), 7.57-7.12 (m, 20H,
PPh2). Anal. Calcd for C50H54FeN2P2: C, 74.99; H, 6.80; N, 3.50. Found:
C, 74.54; H, 6.66; N, 3.39.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction, product depends on stoichiometry
